{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Assess resolution and recurrence protection per target, emphasizing operational safety and simplification: concurrent child isolation, signal/timeout semantics, output streaming, manifest maintainability, bounded inspect/GC authority, exact reclaimed counts, packaging behavior, and whether new mechanisms are riskier than the bug.","packet_sha256":"d2a196cffe726c5a0ef04f4da5f5d9912e4dbd414ce7ea76e43552e1f591c93e","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"e2903a3d6e63ffaae7abc7cd11e43d69fa9d6b116d9238e83148d9b1e160683e","verdict":"block","target_observations":[{"target":"corca-ai/charness#813","verdict":"block","summary":"The repair migrates the evidenced producers to receipt-bound roots and supplies useful lifecycle, GC, and inventory tests, but recurrence protection is not approval-ready. The manifest gate permits any detected production directory creator to bypass ownership by declaring `test-compatibility-only`, and the packet contains no executed evidence for packaging, full-repository inventory, concurrent children, or evaluator signal/streaming behavior.","evidence":["`validate_inventory` excludes every detected directory whose declared disposition is `test-compatibility-only` from `raw_directories`; it does not restrict that disposition to test or compatibility paths.","The spec fixes the opposite rule: production directory roots require receipt-bound ownership and a new creator cannot select a local-cleanup exemption merely because ordinary cleanup exists.","The negative-control test uses `scripts/fixture.py` with `test-compatibility-only` and asserts success, demonstrating that the gate accepts the exemption based only on manifest text, not semantic scope.","Standalone adapter tests cover success, failure, timeout, and cancellation and verify empty registry readback, while scratch tests independently compute reclaimed entry and byte counts and exercise bounded refusals.","The packet lists packaging, agent-runtime, shell, Python, and standing-pytest validators, but provides no command results or receipts proving they ran against these semantic bytes."]}],"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"high","summary":"The recurrence gate has an unrestricted production escape hatch.","evidence":["In `scripts/gates/check_temp_producer_inventory.py`, `raw_directories` includes directory producers only when their manifest disposition is not `test-compatibility-only`.","No validation ties `test-compatibility-only` to test paths, compatibility fallback symbols, or an independently observable predicate.","`tests/test_temp_producer_inventory.py` explicitly proves a directory under `scripts/fixture.py` passes when assigned that disposition.","Therefore a future raw `mkdtemp`, `TemporaryDirectory`, `mktemp -d`, or `mkdtempSync(tmpdir())` in production can be registered under this disposition and pass, contradicting the stated prevention invariant."],"action":"Make the exemption mechanically bounded—for example, restrict it to an explicit allowlisted path/symbol class or remove it for detected directory producers—and add a negative control showing a production path cannot claim it."},{"id":"F2","severity":"medium","summary":"Behavioral evidence is incomplete for the newly changed evaluator execution mechanism.","evidence":["`run-local-eval-test.mjs` changes Claude output to `stream-json`, persists transcripts, launches detached process groups, and sends SIGTERM immediately followed by SIGKILL after synchronous timeout return.","The supplied tests do not exercise Claude/Codex timeout process-group cleanup, parent cancellation, descendant survival, natural output streaming, transcript parsing under malformed or partial streams, or concurrent evaluator homes.","The shell adapter's process matrix does not establish those separate JavaScript `spawnSync` semantics."],"action":"Add process-level evaluator acceptance for timeout and cancellation with descendants, concurrent isolated homes, transcript streaming/readback, and preservation of expected exit/blocker behavior."},{"id":"F3","severity":"medium","summary":"Packaging and full integration claims are asserted but not evidenced by the packet.","evidence":["The spec says implementation is complete and focused acceptance is passing.","The packet only lists planned sync and verification commands, including plugin export synchronization and committed-packaging validation; it includes no outputs, receipts, or results.","The reviewed paths include export-owned sources but no generated mirrors, making synchronized packaging behavior impossible to establish from the semantic payload alone."],"action":"Provide identity-bound results for the inventory gate over the real repository, focused tests, agent-runtime tests, and both packaging validators after canonical export synchronization."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"GC might sweep arbitrary system temporary directories.","bin":"disconfirmed","disposition":"The spec explicitly keeps GC under registered runtime scratch roots, and supplied scratch tests cover repo mismatch, owner-identity mismatch, worktree-inventory failure, active/unexpired refusal, and dry-run default."},{"concern":"Exact reclaimed counts may be approximate or self-fulfilling.","bin":"supported-with-focused-evidence","disposition":"The GC test independently enumerates descendant entries and file sizes before execution and compares both totals exactly."},{"concern":"Concurrent shell gates share one destructive child directory.","bin":"partially-addressed","disposition":"The shell helper derives invocation-local subdirectories using producer, BASHPID, and RANDOM, reducing collision and cross-removal risk; however no concurrent-process acceptance is supplied."},{"concern":"The adapter buffers child output and hides gate progress.","bin":"partially-addressed","disposition":"`run_owned_scratch_command.py` requests `capture=False`, which indicates inherited streaming, but behavior depends on the unreviewed subprocess guard and is not proven by the supplied tests."},{"concern":"The manifest is inherently too large to maintain.","bin":"not-a-blocker-by-itself","disposition":"Stable path/scope/symbol identities plus stale and missing checks are a reasonable simplification boundary; the blocker is the semantically unrestricted exemption, not row count alone."},{"concern":"Immediate SIGTERM followed by SIGKILL is necessarily unsafe.","bin":"unproven","disposition":"Group termination is appropriate for descendant cleanup, but the absence of grace and lack of process-level evaluator tests prevent approval; the payload does not demonstrate concrete corruption."}],"next_move":"Block resolution until the `test-compatibility-only` escape is mechanically constrained and identity-bound execution evidence covers the real inventory, evaluator process semantics, concurrent isolation, and packaging synchronization.","non_claims":["This review does not infer test execution from test source, spec prose, validator lists, hashes, or a clean working-tree patch identity.","This review does not claim arbitrary pre-existing `/tmp` debris belongs to Charness.","This review does not establish behavior of unreviewed `run_monitored_phase`, runtime-scratch implementation internals, generated plugin copies, or packaging validators.","Goal evidence lineage is not goal-bound, so no Goal Run completion is inferred."]}
